Wooden-Chop

Ingredients: OLD SKOOL JUNGLE & DRUM 'N' BASS + EUPHORIC, ENERGETIC & JOLLY + Double Bass + 2020s ERA
Creative Catalyst: A sun-warped 1994 jungle tape, baked in a time capsule and dug up in a Bristol allotment, revealed its sub-bass had entirely rotted into a woody, acoustic resonance.

Wooden-Chop takes the kinetic, hyper-kinetic breakbeats of 1990s rave culture and anchors them to the physical, micro-miked thrum of an upright double bass. Instead of digital sub-drop sine waves, the low-end is generated by aggressive pizzicato plucks, wooden body-slaps, and bow-dragged sub-harmonics. Over this acoustic foundation sits high-gloss 2020s modern production: hyper-bright piano riffs, pitch-shifted pop vocal chops, and euphoric chord progressions that radiate uninhibited joy. It feels simultaneously like a muddy outdoor festival in 1995 and a pristine modern club track, balancing organic warmth with heart-pounding drum and bass energy.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 168–174 BPM. frantic, syncopated Amen and Think breaks layered over a swinging, tactile 4-bar double bass walking line.
- Harmonic Palette: Major 7th chords, Lydian mode brass stabs, and warm, woody root notes played on raw gut strings.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Acoustic Sub-Transplant: Replacing standard 808 subs with low-pass filtered, compressed double bass bow-drones.
  2. Cassette-Bake Saturation: High-end air saturated through simulated magnetic tape oxide wear to smooth out 2020s digital harshness.
  3. Micro-Miked Finger-Snaps: Upright bass string-slaps isolated and routed into multi-tap delays as secondary percussion.
- Dynamics: Explosive drop-ins following breakdown sections featuring soloed double bass passages that build into massive, celebratory wall-of-sound choruses.

Scene & Origin Lore
Born out of the damp outdoor free-parties around the Avon Gorge in 2022, Wooden-Chop was pioneered by rogue jazz conservatoire dropouts and veteran pirate radio operators. The scene was ignited when a degraded 1994 tape was recovered from a local park capsule; its ruined low-end forced producers to record a live double bass to fill the missing frequencies, accidentally discovering a ridiculously bouncy, joyful kinetic energy. Fashion in the scene mirrors this high-low contrast: vintage oversized 90s windbreakers paired with bespoke tweed waistcoats, and heavy-duty hiking boots designed for dancing in knee-deep woodland mud. Party-goers gather around custom-built wooden speaker stacks powered by solar rigs, tossing pinecones onto the DJ booth during high-energy track drops as an informal gesture of respect.

Instruments & Sound Generator Tools
- Upright Double Bass: The core engine, heavily micro-miked at the bridge, delivering both the sub-bass foundation and percussive body slaps.
- 1990s Breakbeat Libraries: Classic sampled breaks (Amen, Assembly Line, Trammen) sliced and re-ordered in modern software.
- Korg M1 Piano Synthesizer: Delivering iconic, bright 90s house and rave chord stabs.
- Granular Sampler Engines: Used for transforming 2020s pop vocals into shimmering, euphoric vocal pads and soaring hooks.

For Fans Of: Roni Size & Reprazent, High Contrast, Shy FX, Nia Archives

